{
  "title": "agent.completions.message.DeveloperMessageExpression",
  "description": "Expression variant of [`DeveloperMessage`] for dynamic content.",
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "content": {
      "description": "A value that can be either a literal or an expression.

This allows Function definitions to mix static values with dynamic
expressions. During compilation, expressions are evaluated while
literal values pass through unchanged.

# Example

Literal value:
```json
"hello world"
```

JMESPath expression:
```json
{"$jmespath": "input.greeting"}
```

Starlark expression:
```json
{"$starlark": "input['greeting']"}
```",
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "description": "An expression (JMESPath or Starlark) to evaluate.",
          "$ref": "functions.expression.Expression"
        },
        {
          "description": "A literal value.",
          "$ref": "agent.completions.message.SimpleContentExpression"
        }
      ]
    },
    "name": {
      "description": "A value that can be either a literal or an expression.

This allows Function definitions to mix static values with dynamic
expressions. During compilation, expressions are evaluated while
literal values pass through unchanged.

# Example

Literal value:
```json
"hello world"
```

JMESPath expression:
```json
{"$jmespath": "input.greeting"}
```

Starlark expression:
```json
{"$starlark": "input['greeting']"}
```",
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "description": "An expression (JMESPath or Starlark) to evaluate.",
          "$ref": "functions.expression.Expression"
        },
        {
          "description": "A literal value.",
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}

